[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Sutton pension fund reports regulatory breaches after missing legal deadlines","lead":"Sutton Council's pension fund has reported breaches to The Pensions Regulator after missing legal deadlines for the McCloud Remedy, which addresses age discrimination in public service pensions. The fund missed a 31 August 2025 deadline for implementing the remedy, affecting 3,544 members. A second breach occurred when the fund issued Annual Benefit Statements by the 31 August 2026 deadline but could not include required McCloud benefit calculations for 2,124 members, due to software delays from its pension administration system provider. By late August, pension administration performance had deteriorated: 45.1 per cent of cases were overdue, against a target of 10 per cent. The fund prioritized death benefit and retirement payments to maintain legal compliance.","iso":"2026-09-29","paper_title":"Pension Administration Projects Update","paper_url":"https://sutton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96666/96666.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Pension Committee","paper_title":"Pension Reforms Update","paper_url":"https://sutton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96676/96676.pdf","headline":"Pension Fund 91.7% pooled through London CIV with Investment Management Agreement signed May 2026","detail":"As at 30 June 2026, 91.7% of Sutton's pension fund (\u00a3785.4m direct through LCIV pooled funds and \u00a3263.1m indirect through LGIM passive funds) was under pooled management. An Investment Management Agreement with London CIV, signed in May 2026, gives LCIV full control over strategy implementation while Sutton retains strategic decision-making. The remaining 8.3% consists of legacy property and infrastructure funds nearing the end of their life.","category":"other","matters":"Asset pooling compliance affects fund management efficiency and cost structure. Sutton's progress towards full pooling demonstrates effective implementation of regulatory requirements and reduces fund operational risk.","figures":"\u00a3785.4m direct LCIV; \u00a3263.1m indirect LGIM; 91.7% pooled; IMA signed May 2026","quote":"As at 30 June 2026 the Fund had \u00a3785.4m invested directly in LCIV pooled funds and \u00a3263.1m invested indirectly through the LGIM passive funds, which represents 91.7% of the Pension Fund's assets under LCIV management.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Pension Committee","paper_title":"Pension Reforms Update","paper_url":"https://sutton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96676/96676.pdf","headline":"First Independent Governance Review must be commissioned and completed by March 2028","detail":"Sutton must commission and complete an Independent Governance Review (IGR) by March 2028, assessing business planning, risk management, Pension Regulator Code compliance, and statutory policies. Any resulting action plan must be submitted to the Secretary of State. The council is incorporating this into its 2027 business plan.","category":"governance","matters":"Systematic independent review of governance, planning and risk management demonstrates regulatory oversight and accountability. This new requirement shows strengthened scrutiny of the pension fund and reduces undisclosed risk.","figures":"Completion deadline: March 2028","quote":"Administering Authorities must commission and complete the first periodic IGR by March 2028. The review should, as a minimum, review business planning, risk management, TPR Code compliance and an assessment of all statutory policies.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Pension Committee","paper_title":"Pension Reforms Update","paper_url":"https://sutton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96676/96676.pdf","headline":"New Senior LGPS Officer and Independent Person must be appointed by 31 December 2026","detail":"Sutton must appoint a named Senior LGPS Officer with statutory responsibility for managing all pension fund functions by 31 December 2026; the role cannot be combined with Section 151 Officer or Head of Service positions and must command the majority of the officer's time. An Independent Person must also be appointed by the same deadline to provide independent advice and scrutiny to the Senior Officer and Pension Committee.","category":"governance","matters":"Governance structure directly affects council accountability and decision-making quality. These appointments demonstrate implementation of new regulatory requirements and strengthen independent oversight of the pension fund.","figures":"Appointment deadline: 31 December 2026","quote":"Funds must designate a specific (named) senior officer with statutory responsibility for managing all of the pension fund functions. The role must operate at a senior leadership level and it cannot be combined with the Section 151 Officer role or the Head of Paid Service. The appointment must be made by 31 December 2026.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Pension Committee","paper_title":"Appendix A - Draft LBS Pension Fund Annual Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://sutton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96669/96669.pdf","headline":"Pension fund asset base exceeded \u00a31.08 billion in 2025-26 with \u00a3102.4m annual growth and \u00a3268.9m growth over five years","detail":"Fund assets increased from \u00a3979m to \u00a31,081m in 2025-26, a gain of \u00a3102.4m (10.4% annual growth). Over five years, fund value has increased \u00a3268.9m. Growth reflects positive investment returns (9.1%) combined with net positive contribution flows (\u00a319.2m), strengthening the financial position available to support pension obligations.","category":"other","matters":"Growing pension fund assets reduce long-term contribution burden on the council and materially strengthen the council's balance sheet financial position","figures":"Fund assets 2025-26: \u00a31,081m (up from \u00a3979m); annual growth \u00a3102.4m; 5-year cumulative growth \u00a3268.9m; annual return 9.1%","quote":"The table above indicates that the Fund's value has increased by \u00a3268.9m over the past five years.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Pension Committee","paper_title":"Appendix A - Draft LBS Pension Fund Annual Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://sutton.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96669/96669.pdf","headline":"Pension fund completed connection to national Pensions Dashboard ahead of statutory deadline with 96% data quality scores","detail":"The London Borough of Sutton Pension Fund successfully connected to the national Pensions Dashboard digital ecosystem ahead of the statutory deadline. Data quality scores achieved 96% for both common data and scheme-specific data, representing substantial improvement from prior years and demonstrating high-quality pension member record management and administration.","category":"governance","matters":"Regulatory compliance and ahead-of-schedule delivery of mandated pensions administration requirements reduces compliance breach risk and demonstrates effective governance","figures":"Data quality 96% for common data; 96% for scheme-specific data; connection completed ahead of statutory deadline","quote":"The London Borough of Sutton Pension Fund successfully completed its connection to the national digital ecosystem ahead of the statutory deadline","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-13"},"name":"Sutton","findings_total":102,"news_drafts_total":1}}